  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city of Venice is built on more than 100 small islands in the marshy lagoon along the Adriatic Sea. The canals, which are up to 10 meters deep, were originally dug as a defence system against invaders. Over time, they have become an integral part of the city's unique beauty and charm. Today, many Venetians still rely on these waterways for transportation, while tourists flock to the city to admire its stunning architecture and romantic atmosphere.\n\nThe city's famous St Mark's Square is surrounded by ornate Byzantine mosaics and golden domes. The square is also home to the Basilica di San Marco, which houses a collection of priceless relics and artworks. Visitors can explore the Doge's Palace, the former residence of the Venetian rulers, and learn about the city's rich history.\n\nDespite its beauty, Venice faces many challenges in the modern era. Rising sea levels threaten to flood the city, while over-tourism puts pressure on the local infrastructure. In recent years, the city has implemented measures to reduce its carbon footprint and promote sustainable tourism practices.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is unique about Venice's location?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It is built on a single large island\", \"It is surrounded by mountains\", \"It is built on more than 100 small islands in a lagoon\", \"It is located near the Mediterranean Sea\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It is built on more than 100 small islands in a lagoon\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What was the original purpose of digging the canals?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To provide transportation for tourists\", \"To create a defence system against invaders\", \"To build homes for Venetians\", \"To promote sustainable tourism practices\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To create a defence system against invaders\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is one of the main reasons why tourists visit Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To learn about its history and culture\", \"To admire its stunning architecture and romantic atmosphere\", \"To try local cuisine\", \"To shop for souvenirs\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To admire its stunning architecture and romantic atmosphere\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is a potential threat to Venice's existence?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Over-tourism\", \"Rising sea levels\", \"Avalanches\", \"Earthquakes\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Rising sea levels\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards Venice?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical and disapproving\", \"Neutral and informative\", \"Positive and admiring\", \"Sarcastic and mocking\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Neutral and informative\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
